## 4. OSINT intent templates

Use `TwitterOsintTemplates` for all standard OSINT tasks.
Do NOT write raw queries inline — use the builder for operator safety.

```python
from datetime import date, timedelta
from src.tools.twitter_query_builder import TwitterOsintTemplates, TwitterQueryBuilder

# Company monitoring — 3 variants returned
queries = TwitterOsintTemplates.company_mentions("Acme Corp", days_back=30)

# Breach/leak monitoring — high-signal queries
queries = TwitterOsintTemplates.breach_leak_monitor("acmecorp.com")

# Protest / hashtag campaign (Bellingcat use case #1)
queries = TwitterOsintTemplates.hashtag_campaign(
    "June3Coup", language="my", min_engagement=10
)

# Person research — from/to/mentions variants
queries = TwitterOsintTemplates.person_research(
    "John Doe", handle="johndoe_handle"
)

# Geo-event with media evidence (keyword + near / geocode via template args or TwitterInput fields)
queries = TwitterOsintTemplates.geo_event(
    ["protest", "demonstration"],
    location="Dhaka",
    radius="10km",
    has_media=True,
    since=date(2024, 6, 1),
    until=date(2024, 6, 15),
)

# Crisis-style monitoring with default tighter radius
queries = TwitterOsintTemplates.location_crisis_monitor(
    ["flood", "evacuation"],
    near_place="chennai",
    radius="15mi",
    since=date.today() - timedelta(days=3),
)
```

